 "title": "LTV-217-G series: single-channel phototransistor photocoupler, halogen-free, half-pitch 4-lead SMD",
 "source": {
  "document": "DS70-2009-0016",
  "revision": "Revision A, effective 09/06/2012",
  "pages": 12
 },
 "summary": "A one-channel photocoupler: an infrared LED on pins 1 and 2 drives a phototransistor whose collector and emitter come out on pins 4 and 3. The body is a halogen-free surface-mount package of four gull-wing leads on a 1.27 mm pitch. Current transfer ratio at IF = 5 mA, VCE = 5 V is sorted into ranks A (80-160 %), B (130-260 %), C (200-400 %) and D (300-600 %); across all ranks and unmarked parts it spans 50-600 %. Input-to-output isolation is rated 3000 Vrms AC for one minute as an absolute maximum, and the LTV-217 series is given an isolation voltage of 3.75 kVrms.",
 "key_figures": [
