   "description": "Setup for the switching times. A pulse drives the LED anode; the cathode goes to ground through a series resistor. The collector is pulled up to VCC by the load resistor RL and is the measured output VCE; the emitter is grounded. While IF is on, VCE falls; ton, ts and toff are taken against the 10 % and 90 % levels of VCE.",
